				     Pat, this is to confirm our earlier
discussions regarding reduced MWh
				     consumption.

				     The present situation that is not
subject to change is 25 MW "flat" @
				MPC @
				     $54.65/MWh terminating 8/31/05.

				     The other "leg" is a minimum of 8 MW
"flat" @ MPC @ Mid-C Index plus
				(+)
				     $.25/MWh terminating 9/30/02.

				     Out of the 8 MW minimum obligation, the
EPMI Trader has agreed to
				reduce
				     and financially settle on a
pre-schedule basis any "un-wanted" excess
				     energy at a cost to Smurfit-Stone of
$2.50/MWh for the desired time
				period.

				     Using your request of scheduling a
total of 31 MWs for the month of
				March,
				     25 MW would be priced at $54.65/MWh, 6
MWs would be consumed and
				priced at
				     the MC Index plus (+) $.25/MWh, the
remaining 2 MWs would not be
				scheduled
				     and or consumed, but would be
financilly settled at a cost to
				Smurfit-Stone
				     of $2.50/MWh times the total MWhrs. for
the month of March.  (2MWs x
				$2.50
				     x 744 hours =$3,720).

				     Please confirm your March nomination at
your earliest convenience and
				let
				     me know if you have any questions and
or concerns.

