THREATENED ENFORCEMENT OF PATENT DID NOT VIOLATE Section 2
OF SHERMAN ACT
Threats to enforce a patent for a rotationally molded
plastic bulk container did not violate Sherman Act Section
2, according to a decision by the U.S. District Court of the
Eastern District of Pennsylvania, where there was no showing
that the patent holder possessed market power or engaged in
anticompetitive conduct ("PennPac International, Inc. v.
Rotonics Mfg. Inc., "E.D. Pa., No. 99-CV-2890, 5/28/01).

