uityAlert.com.     Texas Instruments and RADVISION Team to Offer Fully Inte=
grated Silicon and Software Solutions for IP Phones and Gateways=1DBundled =
VoIP Solution for MEGACO and H.323-based IP Phones and Gateways Enables Fas=
ter Time to Market and Reduced Costs   DALLAS and MAHWAH, N.J., Oct 18, 200=
1 /PRNewswire via COMTEX/ -- Texas Instruments Incorporated (TI) (NYSE: TXN=
), the leader in digital signal processors (DSPs) and software solutions fo=
r voice-over-packet applications, and RADVISION (Nasdaq: RVSN), the leading=
 provider of award-winning, industry-standard products and technology for r=
eal-time voice and video over IP (V2oIPTM), today announced an agreement to=
 bundle RADVISION's MEGACO/H.248 in TI's IP Phone and VoIP residential/smal=
l office home office (SOHO) gateway solutions. TI is already offering RADVI=
SION's H.323 enabling technology in their voice over IP (VoIP) Phone chipse=
t. Customers purchasing a VoIP solution from TI will now have direct access=
 to the RADVISION protocol toolkits that best suit their development needs.=
 This approach shortens new product time-to-market and reduces development =
costs.   "This offering includes all the necessary silicon components, soft=
ware and even a blueprint of how to build your IP Phone or residential/SOHO=
 gateway for manufacturers. This solution will make it simpler, quicker and=
 easier for developers of VoIP communication devices," said Gadi Tamari, CE=
O of RADVISION. "Companies can concentrate on developing unique capabilitie=
s and innovative industrial designs for their devices because programming i=
ntense functionality and intelligence have been developed and integrated fo=
r them in the chipset. The Texas Instruments-RADVISION solution reduces the=
 need for complex engineering and testing which are some of the biggest bot=
tlenecks in developing new technologies."   "TI is dedicated to providing t=
he silicon and software our customers require to address the needs of the V=
oIP market which is why we're working with RADVISION to bundle MEGACO and H=
.323 with our existing solutions," said Bill Simmelink, general manager, Vo=
IP Business Unit at Texas Instruments. "Customers will benefit from the inc=
orporation of RADVISION's protocol toolkits with TI's IP Phone and VoIP gat=
eway solutions to shorten their time-to-market and provide access to best-o=
f-class technologies for their products."   About the Texas Instruments-RAD=
VISION Solution   Both the IP Phone and residential/SOHO gateway solutions =
feature low-power, highly-integrated processors with TI DSP cores, RISC pro=
cessors, and Telogy Software(TM). TI's IP Phone solution features the TMS32=
0C5472 and TI's VoIP codec, and the VoIP residential/SOHO gateway solution =
features the TNETV1010 processor. The TI-RADVISION solution offers manufact=
urers all the system software and support needed for quick and easy develop=
ment of IP Phones and gateways.   TI's Telogy Software products feature a v=
ariety of standards-based packet-network protocols and user interfaces for =
customer applications. The VoIP software includes signaling, telephony and =
protocol-processing modules as well as network-management APIs. The softwar=
e addresses quality-of-service issues, such as network delay, jitter and lo=
st packets, and incorporates compression, line-echo cancellation (G.168-com=
pliant) and tone detection.   Customers can license a specific embedded RAD=
VISION toolkit that meets their development requirements. RADVISION has mod=
els for MEGACO and H.323-based IP Phones and H.323 media gateways and trunk=
ing gateways.   About Texas Instruments   For OEM's developing broadband co=
mmunications solutions, TI's advanced signal processing-based silicon and s=
oftware platforms deliver the optimal performance, lower power consumption,=
 and system level integration required to rapidly deploy differentiated nex=
t generation products for cable modems, digital subscriber line (xDSL) mode=
ms, integrated access devices (IADs), Voice over Internet Protocol (VoIP) g=
ateways, carrier infrastructure, and home and office wireless networking. S=
ee www.ti.com/sc/broadband   Texas Instruments Incorporated is the world le=
ader in digital signal processing and analog technologies, the semiconducto=
r engines of the Internet age. The company's businesses also include sensor=
s and controls, and educational and productivity solutions. TI is headquart=
ered in Dallas, Texas and has manufacturing or sales operations in more tha=
n 25 countries.   Texas Instruments is traded on the New York Stock Exchang=
e under the symbol TXN. More information is located on the web site at http=
://www.ti.com.   About RADVISION   RADVISION is a leading provider of produ=
cts and technology for real-time voice, video, and data communications over=
 packet networks; this includes the Internet and other Internet Protocol (I=
P) based networks. Recognized universally as the experts in real-time voice=
 and video over IP (V2oIP), RADVISION offers the broadest and most complete=
 set of enabling technology and networking systems needed to enable enterpr=
ises and service providers to migrate their voice and video communications =
from traditional telephone networks to new converged networks. Today, hundr=
eds of thousands of end-users around the world communicate over next-genera=
