The holiday season is officially upon us, and we know how frantic life in the
City can become this time of year. With that in mind, we thought you might
like to know about some chamber music concert coming up in the next couple of
weeks -- the perfect escape from the pressures of the season.

The FINE ARTS QUARTET will perform two different programs this weekend at
Bargemusic. On Saturday, November 24, the program includes works by
Mendelssohn and Bruckner; and on Sunday, November 25, works by R. Evans,
Dohnanyi and Mendelssohn.

Bargemusic
http://www.culturefinder.com/calendar/organization?id=111

On Monday, November 26, The ST. LAWRENCE STRING QUARTET performs an
all-Tchaikovsky program at The Metropolitan Museum of Art's Grace Rainey
Rogers Auditorium. The GUARNERI STRING QUARTET also performs at the Met on
Saturday, December 1, with a program of Beethoven, Lutoslavski and Schumann.

Metropolitan Museum of Art
http://www.culturefinder.com/calendar/organization?id=656

The COSMOPOLITAN CHAMBER PLAYERS will be at Merkin Concert Hall on Wednesday,
November 28, performing works by Bach, Schubert and Stravinsky. On Sunday,
December 2, Merkin presents the UREUK CHAMBER ORCHESTRA Orchestra in an
all-Brahms program.

Merkin Concert Hall
http://www.culturefinder.com/calendar/organization?id=651

And last but not least, Mannes College of Music presents the ORION STRING
QUARTET at Mannes Concert Hall on Friday, November 30, performing an
all-Beethoven program.

Mannes College of Music
