With Gold and Silver shining, commodity futures finished
the week on a high note.  Profittaking snapped two winning
stock market sessions, while Treasuries rose and the
Dollar declined on signs the economic economic recovery
will be slow going.  Meanwhile, sparks flew in the Energy
markets as a huge oil facility fire in Kuwait touched off
sharp advances that pushed Crude Oil to new highs for the
week.  Hogs and Bellies advanced, Cotton sizzled to its
best levels in two weeks, and Coffee staged a late rebound
from new lows.  Elsewhere, Cocoa ended quietly higher and
the Grains & Oilseeds complex was dull and boring, with
no fresh news to stir the markets into action.

