quityAlert.com.     FranklinCovey Brings Healing Message of ``Managing Chan=
ge in the Face of Crisis'' to Yahoo! Broadcast=1DFree Webcast Featuring Ste=
phen R. Covey to Help Families and Businesses Cope With Sept. 11 Tragedy No=
w Available On Demand   SALT LAKE CITY, Oct 29, 2001 (BUSINESS WIRE) -- Fra=
nklinCovey (NYSE: FC), a leading global learning and performance solutions =
firm, Monday announced an agreement with Yahoo! Inc. (Nasdaq: YHOO), a glob=
al Internet communications, commerce and media company, to exclusively broa=
dcast a program to help people around the world recover in the aftermath of=
 the recent terrorist attacks on America.   The webcast, presented by Compa=
q, is now available on demand on Yahoo!(R) Broadcast (http://broadcast.yaho=
o.com) through Nov. 16.   Viewers can experience highlights from a two-day =
conference, which was hosted by FranklinCovey at the Sheraton Hotel and Tow=
ers in New York on Oct. 18 and 19 and featured Dr. Stephen R. Covey, vice c=
hairman of FranklinCovey and author of the best-selling book, "The 7 Habits=
 of Highly Effective People."   The conference offers an uplifting and enco=
uraging message to communities, families, organizations and businesses that=
 continue to be affected by the tragic events of Sept. 11. The program incl=
udes addresses by Covey and other inspiring FranklinCovey speakers about th=
e challenging circumstances and issues facing people today.   Covey said, "=
FranklinCovey is extremely appreciative of Yahoo!, which has made it possib=
le for millions of individuals around the globe to view this webcast. Indiv=
iduals and organizations throughout the country and the world are now faced=
 with unexpected circumstances that they never imagined.   "However, by fol=
lowing simple principles and reorganizing priorities, I firmly believe that=
 any person or company can establish a short- or long-term plan, which will=
 allow them to cope with and overcome any hardship and turn it into a succe=
ss."   "The Internet has proven to be a crucial medium to help people conne=
ct with each other and get the latest news and updated videos in the afterm=
ath of the Sept. 11 tragedy," said David Mandelbrot, vice president and gen=
eral manager, Yahoo! Entertainment.   "Yahoo! continues to encourage people=
 to offer assistance to those directly affected by the terrorist attacks an=
d we hope this free program on Yahoo! Broadcast will give families and busi=
nesses around the world the inspiration and strength they need to move forw=
ard during these uncertain times."   During the "Strengthening Families" wo=
rkshop on Oct. 18, Covey used the 7 Habits(R) as a foundation to discuss ho=
w families, through a powerful framework of timeless principles, might enab=
le family members to effectively communicate about and resolve their challe=
nges.   The "Managing Change in the Face of Crisis and Economic Uncertainty=
" conference for businesses and organizations on Oct. 19 featured keynote a=
ddresses by Covey, Bob Whitman, chief executive officer of FranklinCovey, a=
nd Hyrum W. Smith, vice chairman of FranklinCovey and author of "What Matte=
rs Most: The Power of Living Your Values." The program, now available on Ya=
hoo! Broadcast, features highlights from both conferences.   This webcast i=
s presented by Compaq (NYSE: CPQ), a leading enterprise solutions provider,=
 which is making it possible for people around the world to experience this=
 important event.   Yahoo! Broadcast is an entertainment destination, enabl=
ing people to experience the most compelling content available on the Web, =
including interactive audio, video, and other multimedia content from leadi=
ng providers -- in real time and on-demand.   Yahoo! Broadcast works with t=
hree windows; video plays in an upper left window, while related informatio=
n is presented on the right, and a Web browser that allows people to surf Y=
ahoo! Broadcast -- or any other destination on the Web -- is displayed in t=
he lower half of the screen.   About FranklinCovey Co.  FranklinCovey Co. i=
s a leading learning and performance services firm assisting professionals =
and organizations in measurably increasing their effectiveness in leadershi=
p, productivity, communication and sales. Clients include 80 of the Fortune=
 100, more than three-quarters of the Fortune 500, thousands of small- and =
mid-sized businesses, as well as numerous government entities.   Organizati=
ons and professionals access FranklinCovey services and products through co=
nsulting services, licensed client facilitators, one-on-one coaching, publi=
c workshops, catalogs, more than 150 retail stores, www.franklincovey.com a=
nd www.franklinplanner.com. More than 3,500 FranklinCovey associates provid=
e professional services and products in 44 offices in 38 countries.   Yahoo=
