quityAlert.com.     Yahoo! Broadcast Unveils New Television, Movie and Musi=
c Programming=1DSigns Syndication Deal with Carsey-Werner Distribution; Fea=
tures Exclusive Webcasts from Dr. Stephen Covey and Sting; Announces Agreem=
ent with allFOOD.com   LOS ANGELES, Oct 29, 2001 (ENTERTAINMENT WIRE) -- To=
day at the Webnoize 2001 conference, Yahoo! Inc. (Nasdaq:YHOO - news), a le=
ading global Internet communications, commerce and media company, unveiled =
new programming available on Yahoo!(R) Broadcast (http://broadcast.yahoo.co=
m). This new programming consists of an ever-greater variety of television,=
 movie and music content that further establishes Yahoo! as a leading enter=
tainment destination, while also making it more valuable to advertisers.   =
"One of the largest broadband audiences in the world knows to come to Yahoo=
! for entertainment," said Marc Montoya, general manager, Yahoo! Broadcast.=
 "As an independent media company, we are providing consumers with the kind=
 of television, movie and music programming that is not available anywhere =
else on the Web. This reinforces Yahoo! as a valuable destination for users=
, advertisers and marketers."   Yahoo! streams more than 12.9 million hours=
 of rich media to its 210 million monthly consumers. Entertainment enthusia=
sts from around the world have 24-hour access to a variety of channels on Y=
ahoo! Broadcast such as television, movies, music, food, sports, radio, tra=
vel and comedy. The new content includes: full-length television episodes a=
s well as clips from Carsey-Werner Distribution, LLC ("CWD"); an exclusive =
Webcast from FranklinCovey's "Managing Change & Strengthening Families" con=
ference in New York, featuring Dr. Stephen R. Covey; a private Sting concer=
t recorded in Italy; and selected recipe and cooking technique videos from =
allFOOD.com.   Now Showing On Yahoo! Broadcast -- First Syndication Deal An=
nounced   Yahoo! Broadcast and CW eDistribution LLC, the Internet distribut=
ion arm of CWD, are teaming up to provide full-length television episodes a=
s well as popular television clips from the CWD library. Content available =
to consumers on Yahoo! Broadcast includes full-length episodes from the sit=
com "Townies" starring Molly Ringwald, Jenna Elfman and Lauren Graham; as w=
ell as selected clips from classic commercials, celebrity interviews, comed=
y television, movie clips, golf tips, extreme cliffhangers, and selected mu=
sic videos from current to classics.   "We are pleased to provide our compe=
lling content to Yahoo!'s vast worldwide audience," said Robert E. Raleigh,=
 president, Domestic Television Distribution, for CWD. "Yahoo! enables us t=
o engage people on a new level. It is the ideal platform for people to see =
shows that they might not otherwise be able to access. There is a wide vari=
ety of programming that, for one reason or another, cannot be found on TV b=
ut which is nevertheless very popular with certain audiences. Yahoo! makes =
it possible for us to bring those audiences what they want to see easily an=
d economically."   FranklinCovey Brings Healing Message of Dr. Stephen R. C=
ovey to Yahoo! Broadcast   For the first-time ever, Yahoo! Broadcast is off=
ering consumers on-demand access to a special conference held by FranklinCo=
vey, free of charge, aimed at helping families and businesses recover from =
the September 11 tragedy. Available on Yahoo! Broadcast through November 16=
, people can experience highlights from the two-day conference hosted by Fr=
anklinCovey featuring Dr. Stephen R. Covey, vice-chairman of FranklinCovey =
and author of the best-selling book, The 7 Habits of Highly Effective Peopl=
e. Taped at the Sheraton Hotel and Towers in New York City on October 18 an=
d 19, the conference offers an uplifting and encouraging message to communi=
ties, families, organizations and businesses that continue to be affected b=
y the tragic events of September 11. The program includes addresses by Dr. =
Covey and other inspiring FranklinCovey speakers about the challenging circ=
umstances and issues facing people today.   Yahoo! Broadcast Presents Sting=
 Live From Italy  Sting's remarkable and emotional live concert in Tuscany,=
 Italy, on Tuesday, September 11th, 2001 is now available on demand on Yaho=
o! Broadcast through November 5th. The performance was recorded in front of=
 a select audience of friends and lucky contest winners for an album entitl=
ed ...All This Time, which is scheduled to be released by A?Records in the =
United States on November 20th. Originally intended as a live Webcast on Se=
ptember 11th, Sting and his band decided to limit the worldwide broadcast t=
o a single, moving performance of Fragile, followed by a minute of silence =
in honor of the thousands of people who lost their lives in the terrorist a=
ttacks on America. Following the conclusion of the Webcast, the concert res=
umed and a one-hour edited version of the live performance can now be viewe=
d on Yahoo! Broadcast.   Now Cooking On Yahoo! Broadcast  Now available on =
Yahoo! Broadcast, allFOOD.com is offering food enthusiasts the ability to e=
njoy selected recipe and cooking technique videos from programs featuring w=
orld-renowned culinary experts. Viewers can watch Jacques Pepin -- the clas=
sic and traditional master of French cooking; Nick Stellino in "Cucina Amor=
e"; healthy cooking with Graham Kerr; desserts with Nick Malgieri; vintage =
cooking shows from the 1950s and `60s with the first famous television cook=
, Dione Lucas; and many more. In addition to streaming video content on Yah=
oo! Broadcast, an interactive window provides viewers with more information=
 about the content they're watching, including recipes for printing, compre=
hensive reference materials, links to and information about other food site=
s, newsletters, bulletin boards, and online purchasing of books, food and o=
ther products.   About Yahoo! Broadcast  Yahoo! Broadcast is an entertainme=
nt destination, enabling people to experience the most compelling content a=
vailable on the Web, including interactive audio, video, and other multimed=
ia content from leading providers -- in real time and on-demand. Yahoo! Bro=
adcast works with three windows; video plays in an upper left window, while=
 related information is presented on the right, and a Web browser that allo=
ws people to surf Yahoo! Broadcast -- or any other destination on the Web -=
- is displayed in the lower half of the screen.   About Yahoo!  Yahoo! Inc.=
 is a leading global Internet communications, commerce and media company th=
at offers a comprehensive branded network of services to more than 210 mill=
ion individuals each month worldwide. As the first online navigational guid=
e to the Web, www.yahoo.com is the leading guide in terms of traffic, adver=
tising, household and business user reach. Yahoo! is the No. 1 Internet bra=
nd globally and reaches the largest audience worldwide. The company also pr=
ovides online business and enterprise services designed to enhance the prod=
uctivity and Web presence of Yahoo!'s clients. These services include Corpo=
rate Yahoo!, a popular customized enterprise portal solution; audio and vid=
eo streaming; store hosting and management; and Web site tools and services=
. The company's global Web network includes 24 World properties. Headquarte=
red in Sunnyvale, Calif., Yahoo! has offices in Europe, Asia, Latin America=
, Australia, Canada and the United States.   Note to Editors: Yahoo! and th=
e Yahoo! logo are trademarks and/or registered trademarks of Yahoo! Inc. Al=
l other names are trademarks and/or registered trademarks of their respecti=
ve owners.   CONTACT:          Yahoo! Entertainment                   Linda=
